From 688c22836e54637d574df0ac70407402aa19e7d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: michael tesch <tesch1@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 23:32:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] arm64 SME2 gemm: specialize the ZA transposition, stack
 workspace for small problems, size thresholds

The generic transposition cost 50-80 ns per A panel on partial depth chunks;
compile-time variants (A panels, A scaled, B groups) remove that. Problems
whose packed operands fit in 64 KB use a stack workspace instead of
blas_memory_alloc. Below 20^3 multiply-adds GEMM takes the NEON paths, and
the SME1 direct sgemm keeps row-major problems below 56^3, where it is
faster (Apple M4 Pro measurements).
---
 interface/gemm.c                       |  2 +
 kernel/arm64/sgemm_direct_performant.c |  8 ++--
 kernel/arm64/sme2_gemm_impl.h          | 66 ++++++++++++++++++--------
 3 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

diff --git a/interface/gemm.c b/interface/gemm.c
index 93a74959c..06aa4b3d1 100644
--- a/interface/gemm.c
+++ b/interface/gemm.c
@@ -586,6 +586,8 @@ if (strcmp(gotoblas_corename(), "armv9sme") == 0
 #endif
 )
 #endif //defined dynarch
+/* below about 20^3 multiply-adds the NEON paths win over the cost of entering streaming mode (Apple M4) */
+if ((double)args.m * (double)args.n * (double)args.k >= 8000.)
 {
